th high amazing  chemospores they have  a lower survival probability here i am  looking at all risks  but there is some evidence that when i  look at the high risk of work  that cohort also has a lower survival  probability and so this is  showing some evidence that the  classification  of tumors based on their epigenetic  profiles may allow  uh some prognosis analysis in high-risk  neuroblastoma and this is very important  because as i said  for high-risk neuroblastoma there's no  such a prognosis system yet  and that's what we're working with so i  am  going to and now my talk by showing you  one thing that is really interesting in  my opinion which is the fact that we can  compare  these very different types of diseases  on the right i have  a heat map of um neuroblastoma this is  using the  uh rnac profile of neuroblastoma  sorry if i said this is the left this is  the right the right image  the la in the left side here we have a  heat map  showing the mutational profile of covet  19.  so with the high school students that i  told you we  developed these classification system  of covid19 based on the mutational  profiles  so here what's interesting to note is  that by looking at the frequency of  these mutations we see  some sort of clusterization of the  mutations that are  in the extreme or extreme east  of the earth such as  the samples collected from china also  present  in the bat and the penguin which which  are thought to be the animals  that are um more prominent hosts  of of the virus so really here what i  want to say  is that a computational biology methods  allow us to compare  or to uh have a sense of common analysis  that can be done in in two completely  different diseases such as neuroblastoma  and covid19 so in conclusion  as i said bioinformatics can be used to  study and understand these  two very different diseases and many  other types of different diseases as  we saw in during this presentation  and more specifically in my case  bioinformatics may allow the development  of prognosis system for  high risk near blossom so i would like  to end now  thank you so much for listening
 

